# OpenPass for macOS — NO runtime environment variables (by design)
#
# The native app never reads .env files. This file documents where
# configuration actually lives so the convention is explicit.
#
# Runtime configuration:
# - Server URL + email: entered on the lock screen (editable fields), kept in
#   app preferences/UserDefaults ("openpass.deviceId" for the device ID).
# - Vault keys: in memory while unlocked; the biometric copy is wrapped by a
#   Secure Enclave key in the Keychain (VaultKit KeychainBiometricKeyStore).
# - Wrapped vault keys / KDF params: inside the encrypted vault snapshot
#   (VaultKit VaultFileStore), never in plain config files.
#
# Build-time shell variables ONLY (not read by the app itself):
#
# Xcode developer directory. Needed while `xcode-select` points at Command
# Line Tools; omit after `sudo xcode-select -s /Applications/Xcode.app`.
DEVELOPER_DIR=/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer
#
# Usage:
#   brew install xcodegen
#   bash ../../scripts/build-macos-core.sh
#   DEVELOPER_DIR=/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer xcodegen generate
#   DEVELOPER_DIR=/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer xcodebuild \
#     -project OpenPass.xcodeproj -scheme OpenPassMac -destination 'platform=macOS' build
